WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.913
- Okay, so here we are, another
episode of Eating Your Feed.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.920
Today we're going to make a
flaming wheel of cheesy pasta

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.840
that Adam has challenged me to recreate.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.590
There's a place called Le Petit Paris,

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:14.490
and you have this wheel of cheese that has

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:18.210
the top taken off of it,
some liquor is lit on fire,

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.861
they make a cream sauce,
they dump the pasta in,

00:00:20.861 --> 00:00:22.940
swirl it around, then it's done.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.070
We need to get a wheel of cheese I think.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:29.097
You can get it on William
Sonoma for $2,500,

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.380
Costco, $900.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:36.393
Okay, we're gonna buy a 72-pound,

00:00:36.517 --> 00:00:39.633
$900 wheel of cheese.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.997
The Costco product description says,

00:00:41.997 --> 00:00:45.053
"Features, aged 24 months,

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.207
imported from Italy, extravagant."

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.931
(laughing)

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:52.803
Okay.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:55.453
Alright, we're gonna use the cart.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:59.337
(peaceful orchestral music)

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:10.020
Okay, so here's the package,
80 pound warning on it.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:13.870
So this is Rie, Tasty
producer, chef extraordinaire,

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:16.633
Eating Your Feed designated savior.

00:01:17.455 --> 00:01:19.038
- I cannot lift it.

00:01:20.218 --> 00:01:21.600
(laughing)

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.760
- Today I think I'm
gonna need a lot of help.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:24.593
- [Rie] Okay.

00:01:24.593 --> 00:01:25.426
- [Andrew] Let's open it.

00:01:25.426 --> 00:01:26.259
- It's like Christmas.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:28.783
What?

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.303
- Is this a crap brand?

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:31.783
Zanetti?

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.193
- Says typical Parmesan.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:35.693
- Typical Parmesan.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.103
No this is good, this is the good stuff.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.323
- Ooh.
- Wow.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:42.503
- We got a big wheel of cheese.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:46.270
The next thing I have to
do is chop this lid off.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:47.310
Any concerns?

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:50.537
- Just don't hurt yourself,
it's very difficult to cut.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:54.513
- I'd worry about it slipping
and chopping my finger off.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:57.019
- Yeah, that's my
biggest concern for this.

00:01:57.019 --> 00:01:57.852
(laughing)

00:01:57.852 --> 00:02:00.783
- Okay, day three of the cheese adventure.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.260
There are some very specific
tools that are typically used

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.150
for cutting one of these open.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.543
Instead, we got a bunch of other tools.

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.900
This is more of like a
sandwich spread knife,

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.290
oyster shucker, butter
knife, hammer to kind of try,

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:17.453
you know, and we got cut-safe gloves.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.570
(laughing)

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:23.060
Where do you start?

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.790
I'm gonna go to this little serrated blade

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:26.330
and just to try score.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.789
This is gonna take hours, just this alone.

00:02:28.789 --> 00:02:29.754
Oh, (bleep).

00:02:29.754 --> 00:02:32.460
(metal striking metal)

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:33.357
Oh god.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:39.270
We've struck cheese,
mmm, that smells good.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:41.120
Let's just try doing the oyster sh...

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:45.193
And then just kinda, oh
god, like Leonardo da Vinci.

00:02:45.277 --> 00:02:48.527
(metal striking metal)

00:02:48.638 --> 00:02:49.471
(clanging)

00:02:49.471 --> 00:02:50.304
Cheese break.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.833
Oh, this cheese is so good.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.540
Oh, the smell is like,
it's a smell explosion.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.403
We're just gonna have to pop
the rim off this bad boy.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:03.470
Alright, so we got that
now, look, I'm Cheesus.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.083
Also kinda like a toilet seat.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.010
That's okay though.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:08.040
Yeah, now it's a matter
of just cleaning it up.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.863
Look at this, so pure.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:13.080
(inhaling deeply and with satisfaction)

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:16.043
We have taken out all the top layer.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:17.930
I'm gonna start forming the bowl.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.330
Adam, stop eating cheese,
like, we're good to go.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:24.330
We're ready to start making cheese here.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.080
I want to do a test run
before I have any pasta.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.363
How much cognac do you think I should use?

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.133
- Let's do a quarter cup.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:33.323
- Just a quarter?

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.430
- No, half cup?

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:36.363
- Half a cup.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:38.130
That seems like a good amount.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.243
Why is cognac good for flambé?

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.623
- It has a higher alcohol percentage,

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.753
kind of has a, like, mild sweet flavor.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.160
- So I have my blowtorch.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.850
- Have you done flambé before?

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:50.753
- No, never.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.100
(clicking)

00:03:59.060 --> 00:03:59.973
Is that on fire?

00:03:59.988 --> 00:04:00.821
- [Rie] Mmm mmm.

00:04:00.821 --> 00:04:01.654
No.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:03.693
Oh, it's on fire!

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.143
- Is it? Yay,

00:04:06.166 --> 00:04:07.233
it's gone.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:13.120
You wanna kinda wet
around it, so like it...

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.840
- Soaking a wheel of cheese
with fire right now, Adam.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:18.480
Okay, so there, it's kinda on fire.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.280
I want to scoop it out, I'm nervous

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.433
that we're ruining the cheese.

00:04:21.433 --> 00:04:22.993
Can you see the flame?

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.890
This is a lot of fire.

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:26.763
- What should we do?

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.323
Do you want to extinguish it?

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:31.760
- Yeah, I'm just going to put this

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.533
on top to extinguish it, okay?

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.543
It smells like a cheesy
alcoholic concoction.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.620
- [Rie] We can use it for later.

00:04:43.546 --> 00:04:44.920
(laughing)

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:46.240
- Tastes so bad! Ugh!

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:49.660
Alright, so I'm going to scrape up

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.233
a little bit of this cheese.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.003
Attempt two.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:56.882
- [Rie] Raise it, little by little.

00:04:56.882 --> 00:04:58.215
- [Andrew] Okay.

00:04:58.385 --> 00:05:01.135
(dramatic music)

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.060
Now I'm just going to...

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.393
- Oh, yeah!

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.283
- spread the cheese around, ooo.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.370
Oh man, it's just, like, salty alcohol.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.913
- [Rie] Ugh, more cheese and less brandy.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:19.150
- I wanna carve out the
bowl so that it's shallower,

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:22.790
and that way the alcohol
can all be on fire at once.

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.330
Okay, one tablespoon.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:25.280
- Is it too little?

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.150
- Two tablespoons.
- Oh, yeah.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:30.960
- So I'm weighing out my pasta,

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.400
because I want to do the
same amount every time.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.820
So this time I'm gonna scrape up

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:39.820
a little bit more cheese,
ignite it, pour it in now.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.320
Is it extinguished?

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.520
Looks like it is.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:47.820
- [Adam] I mean, the pasta's hot.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:50.423
- Okay, I'm gonna keep
going with my pasta here.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:54.310
Okay that looks kinda
gnarly at the moment.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:55.960
I think I had too much cheese.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.613
Alright, I'm going to take it out.

00:05:59.453 --> 00:06:01.020
Ugh, it's just alcoholic pasta.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:04.200
- Should I pan-fry it and
see what's gonna happen,

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:07.160
like once we completely
cook off the alcohol?

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.610
- [Adam] Oh, it looks so much better.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:10.829
- Look at that creamy glisten.

00:06:10.829 --> 00:06:13.643
Mmm, basically perfect,

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:15.463
Rie did it, so.

00:06:16.449 --> 00:06:18.320
- I think you can get to this, right?

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:21.080
- Maybe you want to flambé longer time,

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.373
before you adding in the parm?

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:25.580
- Okay, this is what's going to happen.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:28.820
Cook the pasta, and then we
toss it in a pan with butter.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.240
That too much butter?

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.543
- No, there's not such a thing.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:34.290
- That's what I like to hear.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:36.380
And a little bit of starchy water,

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:38.283
get that to, like, a good state.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:41.390
You know, in Westerns, how
there's always a bartender

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:44.433
who's wiping down a mug behind the bar?

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:48.840
I'll start heating the
cognac, two tablespoons,

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.143
get it hot before it's ignited.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:53.430
(laughing)

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:58.430
Okay, there, it's on fire,
we're gonna pour it out, yeah!

00:06:58.529 --> 00:06:59.820
- No hair.
- Can you see that?

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:01.623
You can see the singed parts.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:08.033
Alright, pasta goes in there,
mix it around a couple times,

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:11.253
put it in my eating bowl with some pepper.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:13.913
- It's good.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.080
- Yeah, it's actually really tasty.

00:07:16.527 --> 00:07:19.777
- Oh, it's still a little boozy though.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.293
- Time for the best version yet.

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:26.443
I made the bowl a little shallower,

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:29.563
hopefully, that will help
keep the flambé alive.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.610
This time I think we're going to go with

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.623
three tablespoons of cognac.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:40.603
I'm going to poor it
over my spoon, oh, yeah!

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:43.793
Look at that, it's more alive this time.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:49.045
So I think keeping the cognac
moving around is important

00:07:49.045 --> 00:07:51.230
to making sure all the alcohol burns off,

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:53.480
because when it pools some
of the alcohol is trapped.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.773
'Kay, yeah, that smells good.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:08:00.343
I think the cheese actually
had more opportunity to flambé.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.513
Oh, yeah, look at that!

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:07.623
Just needs a little salt,
actually, how'd I (bleep) that up?

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:10.343
Okay, we're at the final attempt now,

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:11.860
that's why I'm wearing a hat.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:13.440
We're going to make a
cream sauce this time.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:14.273
That's also how they do it

00:08:14.273 --> 00:08:15.550
in the video that we're referencing.

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:18.833
So here's some minced
shallot, grated garlic,

00:08:19.075 --> 00:08:21.203
add some cream into it, ooo, yeah.

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:25.100
This will come together so that
it's a little more flavorful

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:28.000
and for the cheese to have a
little bit more to grab onto.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.950
In the video, he actually
adds a little bit

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:33.100
of Parmesan to his sauce, so
we're going to do that as well.

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:35.450
I'm going to do some light
scraping of the wheel here

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:37.000
to get some more cheese crumbs.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.100
I think my chunks were too big.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:41.493
Four tablespoons for this portion.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:43.540
And then once people get up here,

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.350
and we're ready to do the flambing,

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:47.260
we're gonna turn the
lights down a little bit,

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.603
so that you can see the
flames a little better.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:52.103
Ooh, that's too much.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:57.180
Okay, the lights are down, sauce
is nice, people are coming.

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:01.883
Okay, stand back everybody.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:05.643
Oh yeah!

00:09:05.643 --> 00:09:07.040
- [Woman In Polka Dots] Is it working?

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:07.993
- You tell me.

00:09:08.653 --> 00:09:09.486
- Nice!

00:09:09.486 --> 00:09:11.819
(screaming)

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:19.033
- Yeah, cheesy pasta,
what do you guys think?

00:09:19.861 --> 00:09:22.778
- [Rei] It looks crazy in the dark.

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:25.450
- Okay, so now it's going in there.

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:26.570
- Wow.
- Ooh, yeah.

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:29.020
- [Andrew] And yes, now
it's coming all together.

00:09:29.645 --> 00:09:30.920
- [Woman In Polka Dots] It
sounds like mouth sounds.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:31.870
- Everybody silent.

00:09:32.085 --> 00:09:34.097
(squeaking)

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:35.917
Okay, I got the thumbs
up, so here comes...

00:09:35.917 --> 00:09:37.803
- [Woman In Polka Dots] Ahh, shiny.

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:40.310
- Okay, here's a cheesy pasta,

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:43.283
made in a flaming wheel of cheese.

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:45.822
Is it really good?

00:09:45.822 --> 00:09:46.655
- [Rie] Mmhmm.

00:09:46.655 --> 00:09:47.693
- Alright, I gotta find out.

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:50.850
The first time that you
dump a bunch of liquor

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:54.963
into a $900 wheel of cheese,
and it just kind of sits there,

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:56.640
it's a pretty dark moment.

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:58.450
It's a long way back up from there.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.970
You can definitely achieve the same thing

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:02.120
without actually doing
it in a wheel of cheese,

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:04.651
but come on, wheel of
cheese that's on fire,

00:10:04.651 --> 00:10:07.110
little spoon action, pasta goes in there,

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:09.460
pretty fun and I think
it tastes pretty good.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.513
We figured out how to make this thing.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.913
Now I have a lot of cheese
to share with everybody.

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:17.210
Should we save the bowl so
that we could make more?

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:18.390
You want to see more, right?

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:19.413
- [Everyone] Yeah!

00:10:19.483 --> 00:10:20.547
- [Andrew] Alright, let's do it.

00:10:20.547 --> 00:10:21.630
- [Adam] Yay!

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:26.333
- [Andrew] Oh, yes!

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:31.600
(camera shutter opening and closing)

